  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Slalom, board pass and two give-and-goes",
  "description": "Set up a slalom of three cones a little in from one board and a cone level with the penalty area. Two passers, B and C, stand out on the ice – coaches or players. The players queue below the slalom cones with a ball each.\n\nA slaloms with the ball between the cones, plays the ball off the board and collects it on the other side. A passes to B, rounds the cone at full speed and takes the return from B on the move. A skates about ten metres, passes to C, gets the ball back and skates calmly back to the queue with the ball. The next player starts when A has passed to B.\n\nMirror the course the next round so everything is done the other way. Change passers after a few laps. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Ball close to the stick in the slalom and eyes up between the cones."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Play off the board at an angle so the ball comes out in front of you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Speed up round the cone before the return – take the ball at full speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Pass with soft hands and follow through."
    }
  ],
